      "text": "The fundamentals haven't changed: reliable pipelines, good models, tested data. What changed is who consumes the data. Data platforms now feed AI features directly. Databricks describes Agent Bricks as \"the Databricks agent developer platform\" for building and deploying agents ([Databricks docs](https://docs.databricks.com/aws/en/generative-ai/agent-bricks/)), and Snowflake's documentation lists Cortex AI Functions, Cortex Agents and Cortex Search alongside its warehouse features ([Snowflake AI features](https://docs.snowflake.com/en/guides-overview-ai-features)). Data engineers who can prepare clean, governed, retrievable data for these tools are building on the same core skills, one layer further up."
